    {
      "entryId": "job-19-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Amid intense agony and abandonment, Job makes the monumental confession: \"I know that my Redeemer lives, and He shall stand at the last upon the earth; and after my skin is destroyed, yet in my flesh I shall see God.\" First principle: bodily resurrection and personal vindication through an eternal Kinsman-Redeemer are anchored in the oldest poetry of Scripture.",
      "density": 2.5607,
      "words": 59,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-1-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Naked in, naked out; the name of the LORD blessed anyway. First principle: stewardship of loss — the Giver's rights are acknowledged at the moment of the taking; sin stayed away from the lips.",
      "density": 2.1643,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-33-23",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The interpreter to show man his uprightness. First principle: Elihu names the need — one among a thousand to mediate and interpret; the rarity finds its supply in the one Mediator.",
      "density": 2.1464,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-19-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Worms destroy the body; the eyes see God in flesh. First principle: the resurrection hope is declared from suffering's floor — in my flesh, not as a ghost; Job foresees the renewed body.",
      "density": 2.1393,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-9-33",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Job wishes for an umpire laying a hand on both. First principle: the deepest Old Testament ache — a mediator who can touch God and man; the wish is answered at Calvary.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-42-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "But now mine eye seeth Thee — and Job repents in dust. First principle: hearing-of becomes seeing — the encounter with God converts theology into humility; the second-hand God becomes first-hand.",
      "density": 2.0107,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-9-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "And treadeth upon the waves of the sea. First principle: the Creator alone stretches skies — and the One walking on waves later wears this title in person on Galilee.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-14-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Not one — from the man of Uz. First principle: the inherited-uncleanness question is asked so the new birth can answer it: that which is born of flesh is flesh.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-5-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The froward counsel carried headlong. First principle: Eliphaz's true saying — even from a wrong friend — is Scripture twice over: Paul quotes it against worldly wisdom.",
      "density": 1.9321,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-16-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Job's heaven-side witness while friends accuse. First principle: the earth's court is lost; heaven's record stands — the scintilla of the Advocate doctrine before the Incarnation.",
      "density": 1.7929,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-2-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The second trial answered without lip-sin. First principle: Job refuses the transactional God — receiving both hands from heaven without charging Him foolishly.",
      "density": 1.5464,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "job-38-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The answer comes from the storm, not the argument. First principle: after thirty-one chapters of human speech, God speaks from whirlwind — creation-questions replace creature-complaints.",
